nt given to Sarita, then what amount will Sarita get?", "optionA": "Rs. 3,000", "optionB": "Rs. 30,000", "optionC": "Rs. 5,000", "optionD": "Rs. 4,500", "answer": "D", "solution": "Ratio method"}, {"question": "If 45% of a number is 15 less than 70% of that number, then find that number.", "optionA": "50", "optionB": "60", "optionC": "70", "optionD": "40", "answer": "B", "solution": "0.25x=15"}, {"question": "If the difference between 62% and 80% of a number is 198, find the difference between 92% and 56% of that number.", "optionA": "3564", "optionB": "360", "optionC": "396", "optionD": "1100", "answer": "C", "solution": "x=1100"}, {"question": "Two students A and B were paid a total of ₹ 4,400 as prize money. If A was paid 120 per cent of the amount paid to B, then how much amount (in rupees) was paid to B?", "optionA": "2400", "optionB": "2000", "optionC": "1800", "optionD": "1500", "answer": "B", "solution": "Ratio 6:5"}, {"question": "The income of a man first increased by 20% and then again by 30%. Find out overall percentage increase.", "optionA": "58", "optionB": "54", "optionC": "60", "optionD": "56", "answer": "D", "solution": "1.2×1.3=1.56 ⇒ 56%"}, {"question": "If a number is increased by 20%. Then it is decreased by 10%. Find its net increase or decrease.", "optionA": "8% increase", "optionB": "10% decrease", "optionC": "10% increase", "optionD": "8% decrease", "answer": "A", "solution": "1.2×0.9=1.08 ⇒ 8% inc"}, {"question": "The price of a book was first increased by 25% and then reduced by 20%. What is the change in its original price?", "optionA": "10% increase", "optionB": "No change", "optionC": "5% decrease", "optionD": "10% decrease", "answer": "B", "solution": "1.25×0.8=1"}, {"question": "The salary of an employee first increases by 50% and thereafter decreases by 54%. What was the overall percentage change in his salary?", "optionA": "4% increase", "optionB": "31% decrease", "optionC": "31% increase", "optionD": "4% decrease", "answer": "B", "